10
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
27 Dresses is a 2008 American romantic comedy film directed by
Anne Fletcher and written by Aline Brosh McKenna.

11
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:09,000
It stars Katherine Heigl as a woman who has served as a bridesmaid 27 times and faces a turning
point when her younger sister becomes engaged to the man she secretly loves.

12
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:42,000
James Marsden, Edward Burns, Malin Akerman, and Judy
Greer appear in supporting roles.

13
01:12:09,000 --> 01:12:15,000
Produced by Spyglass Entertainment and distributed by 20th Century Fox, the film was conceived
following the success of McKenna's screenplay for The Devil Wears Prada (2006).

14
01:17:42,000 --> 01:17:48,000
Principal photography took place in New York City and
Rhode Island from May to July 2007.

15
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:21,000
27 Dresses premiered in Los Angeles on January 7, 2008, and was
released theatrically in the United States on January 18.

16
01:28:48,000 --> 01:28:54,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise directed at
Heigl's performance and criticism aimed at its formulaic plot.

17
01:34:21,000 --> 01:34:27,000
It emerged as a commercial success, grossing $162.7
million worldwide against a $30 million budget.

18
01:39:54,000 --> 01:40:00,000
The film explores themes of newspaper, new love,
lovesickness, sibling relationship, wedding planner.

19
01:45:27,000 --> 01:45:33,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
